# Binary k-distribution parts (plan R08, R08.T4.d; decision-r08-t4d-kdist-chain.md §9): never diffed,
# merged or normalised as text.
apps/hyperion/src/renderer/src/view/atmosphere/absorbers/kDistributions/*.bin binary
apps/hyperion/src/renderer/src/view/atmosphere/absorbers/exomol/kDistributions/*.bin binary

# hyperion-fit's datasets, hashed byte for byte against their PROVENANCE.toml (plan 14, P14.T49.i;
# splib07a's spectra keep their CRLF line ends): never normalised, so that a checkout with
# core.autocrlf, as on Windows, keeps their bytes.
crates/hyperion-fit/data/** -text

# hyperion-fit's manifests and the fitted tables it writes are LF text, hashed byte for byte: a
# manifest's bytes enter its task's inputs hash, and a table's body its hash in `tables.lock`, so
# that a checkout with core.autocrlf would fail `hyperion-fit check` (plan 14, P14.T49.d and T49.e).
crates/hyperion-fit/manifests/*.toml text eol=lf
crates/*/src/tables/*.rs text eol=lf

# Golden files are LF text, read line by line by the Rust and TypeScript tests; a CRLF checkout
# (Git for Windows' default) would fail every comparison (decision-r10-t16d-part1, item 6).
*.golden text eol=lf
